      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bonaparte began in 1837 as Meeks Mills, a riverside settlement on the Des Moines River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://bonaparte-iowa.com/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1841 William Meek renamed the town Bonaparte, honoring the French emperor he admired.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonaparte%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bonaparte holds the distinction of being the smallest Main Street Community in the United States.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://bonaparte-iowa.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Riverfront Park showcases restored mills, historic lock walls, and a refurbished bandshell beside the river.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://bonaparte-iowa.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Five National Register sites in Bonaparte include the Aunty Green Hotel, Riverfront District, and Meek's Flour Mill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonaparte%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
